--- !u!114 &2030101021
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2030101019}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: '---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    REASON
    FOR CONSULTATION

    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


    Patient
    was referred following repeated episodes of emotional distress, sleep disturbance,
    social withdrawal, and difficulty recalling specific periods of childhood.


    Patient
    reports frequent nightmares and discomfort when left alone for extended periods.


    When
    asked about her childhood home, the patient became noticeably quiet and avoided
    further discussion.


    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    BACKGROUND

    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


    Patient
    describes spending extended periods isolated inside the family home during childhood.


    She
    reports having limited opportunities to leave the house freely or interact with
    other children.


    Patient also recalls repeated bullying from

    children
    of a similar age.


    Details regarding the family environment remain unclear.


    When
    questioned about her parents, the patient showed visible discomfort and requested
    to change the subject.


    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    MEMORY
    OBSERVATION

    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


    Patient
    demonstrates difficulty recalling several periods of her childhood.


    Some
    memories appear fragmented or incomplete.


    Patient is able to remember specific
    objects,

    places, and conversations, but has difficulty

    placing them
    in chronological order.


    Certain memories appear to trigger strong

    emotional
    reactions despite the patient being unable to explain the events clearly.


    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    FAMILY
    RELATIONSHIP

    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


    One
    name appears repeatedly throughout the patient''s recollections:


    Evelyn.


    Older
    sister.


    When discussing Evelyn, the patient''s behaviour changes noticeably.


    Patient
    describes her sister as the person she felt safest with during childhood.


    Several
    positive childhood memories described by the patient involve Evelyn:


    reading
    together before bed,

    playing inside their room,

    and talking late at
    night when the rest of the

    house was quiet.


    Patient stated:


    "When
    Evelyn was there,

    I wasn''t scared."


    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    SESSION
    NOTE

    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


    During
    the session, the patient was asked:


    "Do you feel safe at home?"


    The
    patient remained silent.


    After approximately twenty seconds, she asked:


    "Is
    Evelyn coming back?"


    No further response was given.


    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    FOLLOW-UP
    SESSION

    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


    Patient
    became increasingly distressed when the topic of separation from her sister was
    discussed.


    When asked about the last time she saw Evelyn, the patient stated
    that she could not remember clearly.


    After a prolonged pause, she added:


    "She
    promised."


    Patient refused to elaborate.


    Further questioning was
    discontinued.


    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    ADDITIONAL
    OBSERVATION

    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


    The
    patient appears to associate Evelyn strongly with feelings of safety and protection.


    Memories
    involving separation remain particularly difficult for the patient to discuss.


    Continued
    observation is recommended.


    Further sessions should proceed carefully when
    discussing childhood memories or family relationships.


    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    END
    OF RECORD

    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------'
